# The Preferences window (PrefWin, see src/ui/prefwin.c; opened by MENU, GAME, Preferences...): as it opens, the hover looks of a tab, an
# option and a button, every page of the group of tabs (Preferences, Adv., Warning, Automation, Audio/Visual, Map), the Warning page
# and the More and Fewer buttons that swap its box for a second, and Cancel. The state regions are the window's own words (the page, the
# eleven option words), each box's dialog (its count, position, selection and hover), the four sliders' positions, the four sound
# buttons' states, the visible flag of each box, slider and button a page shows and hides, the tabs' ButtonGroup, the game's preference words and what the window hands over, and the sound object's two
# channels (the object itself holds pointers that differ from run to run).
